+ SCOPE AND START (amendment, before start). SCOPE NARROWING: rust-1 is narrowed to arm L alone (L-R and L-C, all four builds of each, on every host where this bar lists arm L), which serves the IMPLEMENTATION answer (speed and memory). The library and engine arms G-OB, G-MKL, T, Q and X, the Candle extra, the FRAMEWORK and KERNELS answers, Band W, the FRAMEWORK and KERNELS lines of LABELS FOR EVERY OUTCOME, the FRAMEWORK and KERNELS lines of EXPECTED VALUES, item (2) of the TRUST COLUMN, the library-arm parts of WALL CLOCK AND COST CAP, the FRAMEWORK and KERNELS sentences and the framework and engine clauses of the headline sentence are NOT IN FORCE for rust-1. They are not deleted from the text above (the registered text is kept whole); they are carried unchanged, with every threshold and INVALID condition, into the bar of a separately registered experiment, rust-1b, which has its own pass mark, is registered and public in the fingerprint ledger before any of its runs, and carries its own freeze sha256 in its own start --ref. The single result of rust-1 is the arm L label (IMPLEMENTATION speed and memory); it is recorded when the arm L jobs have been verified. No FRAMEWORK or KERNELS statement may be drawn from rust-1, and the headline sentence of rust-1 reads "implementation: <label>." Arm L keeps its label rule (Band S and its boundaries, the faster-of-two-opt-levels rule, 5 reps and the single redo as 10), its INVALID conditions, its sentences, its hosts, its memory limits and its caps as registered above, word for word. The FRAMEWORK memory line (peak PSS of G, T, Q, L-R and L-C side by side) belongs to rust-1b, which takes the L-R and L-C rows from rust-1 and says that they were taken earlier. START AND FREEZE: everything that this bar says is recorded and frozen "before the initial timing run" is recorded and frozen for arm L before the initial arm L timing job starts. The freeze record is the file state/reports/rust-lab/rust-1/FREEZE-ARM-L.md; its sha256 (a